Response to the team’s final amendments

Verdict: accept all of them, with four refinements. The scope stays frozen, and the amended specification becomes v1.1.

Where I refined or disagreed
Point	Verdict	Refinement
3. Per-dimension gating	Accept	D1 to D4 each get their own minimum evidence test from the D0 sub-items. A case can show Mechanism: Misaligned alongside Verification: Insufficient evidence.
4. D6 labels	Accept	The case card carries the fixed sentence “Failure to identify a relevant event is not evidence that no event occurred.”
5. D3/D4 evidence classes	Accept, with a consequence for the rules baseline	See below.
8. Scope coverage	Accept, with a fix to my own wording	See below.
9. LLAC	Accept	“Final required action completion” is retired. A required-action flag, if one exists, becomes an alternative anchor tested in sensitivity.
10. Descriptive temporal design	Accept	I remove “compared against the P1 window” entirely. Periods are shown side by side with observable days and no comparison language.
11. Bedding-in	Accept	30 days is the single pre-registered display configuration. 0 and 90 days are recorded for every case, and no one picks between them after seeing results.
13. Duplicates and bulk	Accept	D6 thresholds apply to deduplicated occurrences. A bulk incident counts as one occurrence and carries a flag. A Severe or Very High member makes the occurrence Severe.
14. Privacy scrubbing	Accept, add a test	Label a sample of cases on original and scrubbed text in the secure layer, and report how often D1 or D2 changes. A material change blocks the scrubbing version.
15. Time boxes	Partly accept	See below.
16. Split G2	Accept	G2C is run as three arms (current process, rules-assisted, AI-assisted) only if G2B shows the model beats the rules. Otherwise it runs as two arms.
17. Outcome codes	Accept	Codes become multi-select, except “No concern identified”, which is exclusive.
18. No-action cohort	Accept	If the pilot has fewer than about 30 such cases, they are reported descriptively with no gate.
19 and 20. Stages and value test	Accept	Stage 3 can start once G1 passes, overlapping Stage 2, because retrieval depends on validated weakness extraction, not on the workflow experiment.

Point 5, and the rules baseline. The team is right that an absent phrase does not establish “not evidenced”. But my B1 baseline used exactly that. Both stand if I separate two things. B1 emits a flag (“no recognised verification term”), which is a screening proxy. A D4 value of “Not evidenced in the record” in the product requires model assessment with expert confirmation. If rules win G2B, the deployed rules product shows the flag wording, not the D4 value.

Point 8, a correction to my own spec. I defined Partial as “some but not all”. That conflicts with silence becoming Unclear. A cleaner structure is a per-element state:

Covered: the record expressly or structurally supports coverage.
Expressly limited: the record names a narrower scope, or the only action covering it was cancelled.
Not established: silence.

Case-level scope is then Complete if all are covered. It is Partial only if at least one element is expressly limited. It is Unclear if the rest are merely not established. Parent-to-descendant process inheritance counts only under an agreed rule or expert confirmation.

Point 15. Agreed for ground-truth labelling: no forced decisions, and “cannot determine within allocated time” is a recorded outcome. I would keep the fixed time box in the G2C workflow arms, because comparing review processes without a common time limit measures nothing. The distinction is that labelling is untimed and the workflow experiment is timed.

Where I would change the plan

1. Sequence the pack so real data is touched first. Fifteen documents before anyone looks at the data is the wrong order, because G0 is the cheapest way to kill the proposition. The data profile and pilot scorecard should run in the first fortnight, in parallel with the drafting.

2. Deliver one artefact at a time. Each one gets your team’s review before the next is built. A fifteen-document drop tends to produce shallow review of all of them.

3. Source-to-target mapping needs your physical schema. I can define logical fields, but not column names. Please send the table and column list (a data dictionary, or even field names only) before artefact 1.

